    "description": "One of the largest animals of the Late Devonian seas, about 370 million years ago: an armoured placoderm that may have reached 5 to 7 metres long. Despite its size and heavy head-and-shoulder armour, its long jaws were small-mouthed and toothless, and it probably cruised slowly through open water filtering out small prey, much like a basking shark. Its sheer bulk made it very hard for any predator to bring down."
