    "description": "A sleek lobe-finned hunter about 1.6 metres long from the Late Devonian rivers of New South Wales, Australia, about 365 million years ago. Torpedo-shaped, with its dorsal and anal fins set far back and a symmetrical tail, it was built for sudden bursts of speed like a modern pike or barracuda. It waited in ambush and shot forward to seize armoured fish in its long, fanged jaws, but its lightly built body could not take much punishment."
