    "description": "A goniatite ammonoid from the Late Devonian seas, about 375 million years ago, so common around the world that it marks a whole stretch of geological time. Its tightly coiled, flattened shell, up to about 15 centimetres across, carried zig-zag suture lines and was more streamlined than those of earlier, loosely coiled ammonoids. It darted backwards by jet propulsion to snatch small prey or escape danger."
